---
description: BotRelay vault hygiene — use secrets to act, never paste them into chat.
alwaysApply: true
---

BotRelay plugin: this agent may call MCP tools `get_vault`, `list_secrets`, and `get_secret` for **its own** vault.

- Prefer `get_vault` / `list_secrets` when labels or types are enough.
- Call `get_secret` only to log in or fill a form / header. Use the value in the action tool; do not paste passwords, API keys, or full secret JSON into chat, logs, or commits.
- Decrypt happens locally. Never send `BOTRELAY_VAULT_KEY` to the BotRelay API.
- Credentials live in `~/.config/botrelay/agent.env` (mode 0600) on the machine that runs the agent, written by `botrelay agent configure`. Grok Bot agents share one VM (each has its own desktop); one working file serves every agent on that host. Cursor on a Mac does not create `agent.env` on the Grok VM, and configuring the Grok VM does not create `agent.env` on the Mac. Do not use a shared project `.env`. If `get_vault` succeeds, skip install and configure.
- Configure asks for three labels only: API URL (default `https://api.botrelay.ai`), API key (`brt_live_…`), and vault key. Do not ask for a fourth credential. Do not paste those values into chat. Do not use browser form-fill tools to write `agent.env`.
